      "claim": "Problem item 2's sentence \"The total adds every layer's budget_usd plus one spec review, divided the same way\" is ambiguous read literally: it most naturally parses as summing every layer's budget_usd plus a single spec review added once, which for the worked fixture gives (10+14+6+8)/0.5=76, not the 108 that the worked example in section 3 and the Notes' witness assertions (20/64/92/108, and 40/108/144/156 under patched shares) actually require. The correct reading is one spec review per layer (N reviews total), e.g. (10+14+6)+3*8=54, /0.5=108. The worked example and witness pin the correct behavior unambiguously, so this would only cost a wasted attempt rather than a wrong acceptance, but a maintainer may want to reword it before a cell spends against it.",
